| info = *Hydroid expends {{Stat|Ability Efficiency|icon=only}}'''50''' [[energy]] to summon a creature from the deep, causing up to <u>'''8 / 12 / 16 / 20'''</u> tentacles to emerge from all surfaces within a marked location {{Stat|Ability Range|icon=only}}'''15 / 15 / 15 / 15''' meters in radius, cast over '''<u>unrestricted</u>''' range. Tentacles prioritize spawning beneath enemies inside the radius, with each tentacle capturing their initial targets and lifting them into the air until the ability expires after {{Stat|Ability Duration|icon=only}}'''10 / 13 / 18 / 20''' seconds. Captured enemies are incapacitated in a {{D|Ragdoll}} state and stay attached to the tentacles while suffering {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''50 / 100 / 150 / 200''' {{D|Corrosive}} Damage with '''<u>100%</u>''' [[status chance]] per second.
*Tentacles will '''not''' capture enemies with crowd control immunity/{{D|Overguard}}, or inflict their {{D|Corrosive}} damage over time, since they are not physically attached. However, such enemies will be attacked '''once''' by the tentacle spawning under them, inflicting {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''50 / 100 / 150 / 200''' {{D|True}} damage with a guaranteed {{D|Corrosive}} status effect.
**Tentacles detect and capture new enemy targets when they come into range. (See [[#Bugs]])
**Each tentacle can only capture '''1''' enemy at a time, for a total of '''20'''.
**Tentacles with captured enemies will hold their victims steady in the air, allowing players to take aim and kill their targets.
*Casting Tentacle Swarm is a two-handed action that stops Hydroid's movement and other actions. 
*Can be recast while active; however, only one instance of Tentacle Swarm can be active at a time. Recasting will replace the previous instance.
*Hydroid briefly summons the Kraken at the center of the spawn area as a visual effect. The Kraken emerges from a pool of water, then submerges slowly and disappears. Kraken is affected by Hydroid's chosen Warframe appearance and energy colors.
*Tentacles appear as translucent water tendrils emerging from a small puddle of water. Tentacles emit splashes of water periodically, as well as a steam particle effect at their base which is affected by Hydroid's chosen Warframe energy color. However, when the ability is cast by {{WF|Hydroid Prime}}, the tentacles will be opaque and more organic in appearance.
| interactions = 
* [[Hydroid/Abilities#Passive|Hydroid's Passive]] allows the first {{D|Corrosive}} stack to remove 50% armor and is able to fully remove all armor at 10 stacks.
** However, Tentacle Swarm alone cannot reach 10 {{D|Corrosive}} stacks and is only able to reach 8 stacks at most due to inflicting status per second and the status effect's 8 second duration.
* {{A|Plunder}}'s {{D|Corrosive}} damage buff applies to Tentacle Swarm's damage.
